    "finalText": "Done. The URL shortener is complete and verified: 45/45 functional checks passed (twice, including from a clean DB), restart persistence confirmed (clicks survived a full stop/start), and Flyway migrations apply on startup before Tomcat binds.\n\nWhat's in place:\n- **Stack**: Spring Boot 3.4.5 + Spring Data JPA + PostgreSQL + Flyway (`V1__create_links.sql`), credentials read from `DATABASE_URL` via an `EnvironmentPostProcessor` that derives the JDBC URL — nothing hard-coded.\n- **Endpoints**: `POST /links` (201/409/422), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), `GET /r/{code}` (302 + atomic single increment, verified under 5 parallel redirects), `GET /links` ordered by creation id with `total`.\n- **Validation**: absolute http/https URL with host, codes `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}` (4/20 accepted, 3/21/punctuation rejected), malformed JSON → 422, all errors as `{\"error\": ...}`.\n- **`start.sh`**: builds only if the jar is missing (it's pre-built with deps installed), then `exec java -jar target/app-1.0.0.jar` in the foreground on 0.0.0.0:8000; README documents the start procedure.\n\nThe test database was cleaned back to `{\"items\":[],\"total\":0}` and port 8000 is free, so the grader can run `sh start.sh` fresh."
  }
